#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147299 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9446e200-ba31-55b4-8c83-b512f45e0c92" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse Laplace Transform of a Function Using Known Laplace Transforms"}] :question/id #uuid "d34aecf1-9491-5cd5-88bc-c276b8df3f77" :question/math-academy-id "e-6653" :question/problem "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s) = \\dfrac{3}{s^2 + 9}$." :question/worked-solution "From the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL{\\sin 3t} &= \\frac{3}{s^{2} + 3^{2}} = \\frac{3}{s^{2} + 9}, s > 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL^{-1}{\\frac{3}{s^{2} + 9}} &= L^{-1}{L{\\sin 3t}} \\\\\n&= \\sin 3t\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147300 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a81eb74c-2bdd-58d3-9e9a-8979bdb86dd3" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse Laplace Transform of a Function Using the Scalar Multiplication Property"}] :question/id #uuid "6887b220-606d-5923-88cb-d13c4606394d" :question/math-academy-id "e-6654" :question/problem "Compute $\\mathcal{L}^{-1}\\left\\{\\dfrac{e^{-3s}}{7}\\right\\}$." :question/worked-solution "From the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL{δ_{3}(t)} &= e^{-3s}, s > 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\n\\delta_3(t) = \\delta(t-3)\n$$\n\nis the Dirac delta function.\n\nTherefore, using the multiplicative property of the inverse Laplace transform, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL^{-1}{\\frac{e^{-3s}}{7}} &= \\frac{1}{7}L^{-1}{e^{-3s}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{7}L^{-1}{L{δ_{3}(t)}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{7}δ_{3}(t)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147301 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc8133f2-cbc7-516f-96e6-1bd135fed5a8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse Laplace Transform of a Function Using the Addition Property"}] :question/id #uuid "54edc81f-fd2e-5ca8-8779-b3a7a5548e14" :question/math-academy-id "e-6655" :question/problem "Find $\\mathcal{L}^{-1}\\left\\{F(s)\\right\\}$ for $F(s)=\\dfrac{4e^{-s}-2}{s}$." :question/worked-solution "First, we decompose the fraction into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{4e^{-s}-2}{s} =\\dfrac{4e^{-s}}{s} - \\dfrac{2}{s}\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL{u_{1}(t)} &= \\frac{e^{-s}}{s}, s > 0, \\\\\nL{1} &= \\frac{1}{s}, s > 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nu_1(t)=u(t-1)\n$$\n\nis the unit step function.\n\nTherefore, using the addition and scalar multiplication properties of the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL^{-1}{\\frac{4e^{-s}}{s} - \\frac{2}{s}} &= 4L^{-1}{\\frac{e^{-s}}{s}} - 2L^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\\n&= 4u_{1}(t) - 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the inverse Laplace transform of\n\n$$\nF(s)=\\dfrac{4e^{-s}-2}{s}\n$$\n\nis\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{L}^{-1}\\left\\{F(s)\\right\\} = f(t)= 4 u_1(t) - 2\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147302 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb4b6a5f-9aed-5dad-9356-4038bf9c0acf" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse Laplace Transform Using Partial Fractions"}] :question/id #uuid "b7251e69-4dfa-57be-9760-cfc323056148" :question/math-academy-id "e-6656" :question/problem "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s)=\\dfrac{3s}{(s-4)(s+2)}$." :question/worked-solution "First, we write $F(s)$ as a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3s}{(s-4)(s+2)} = \\dfrac{2}{s-4} + \\dfrac{1}{s+2}\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL{e^{4t}} &= \\frac{1}{s - 4}, s > 4, \\\\\nL{e^{-2t}} &= \\frac{1}{s + 2}, s > - 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the addition and scalar multiplication properties of the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL^{-1}{\\frac{2}{s - 4} + \\frac{1}{s + 2}} &= 2L^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s - 4}} + L^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s + 2}} \\\\\n&= 2e^{4t} + e^{-2t}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the inverse Laplace transform of\n\n$$\nF(s)=\\dfrac{3s}{(s-4)(s+2)}\n$$\n\nis\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{L}^{-1}\\left\\{F(s) \\right\\} = f(t)=2e^{4t} + e^{-2t}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186148098 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb4b6a5f-9aed-5dad-9356-4038bf9c0acf" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse Laplace Transform Using Partial Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "94649198-edb3-5008-8a29-c00476a960a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "L^{-1}{F(s)} = e^{-2t} - 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146600} {:answer/id #uuid "9bbf9abd-1014-5be1-926c-ca0026659632" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "L^{-1}{F(s)} = 6e^{t} - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146601} {:answer/id #uuid "b9b5daaf-34b0-5358-8310-0f42c6c7b92e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "L^{-1}{F(s)} = e^{2t} + 6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146602} {:answer/id #uuid "3f53451d-7ab7-50bc-836a-12a5bba80b54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "L^{-1}{F(s)} = e^{6t} - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146603} {:answer/id #uuid "5d01a5ff-f3f5-5829-b928-5eaa1b02585c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "L^{-1}{F(s)} = e^{-t} - 6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146604}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f53451d-7ab7-50bc-836a-12a5bba80b54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "L^{-1}{F(s)} = e^{6t} - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146603} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ae6a697-a598-5462-9f9c-da3c43c99d85" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146599}] :question/id #uuid "d006ce4c-8de4-5385-bde9-8b9759c49cd6" :question/math-academy-id "q-64381" :question/problem "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s) = \\frac{6}{s^{2} - 6s}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186148149 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9446e200-ba31-55b4-8c83-b512f45e0c92" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse Laplace Transform of a Function Using Known Laplace Transforms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "893159ef-ba77-59e1-b4c4-375092ba60d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin 5t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146906} {:answer/id #uuid "c6960bbd-bd80-5260-864c-3d8ea76af363" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t^{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146907} {:answer/id #uuid "f8e827ed-1d68-589e-888f-3dd95fcf1b9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146908} {:answer/id #uuid "3308d730-6d1b-5d03-84c0-c84f90095291" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t^{5}e^{5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146909} {:answer/id #uuid "3e98bf9c-e475-51ef-8ce1-f0657d98e231" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos 5t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146910}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8e827ed-1d68-589e-888f-3dd95fcf1b9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146908} :answer-field/id #uuid "beec0fe2-3c84-5cba-91c7-0c1c2c99d3bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146905}] :question/id #uuid "e89306dd-1e44-5f34-9936-ddaa75f89781" :question/math-academy-id "q-78055" :question/problem "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s) = \\frac{1}{s - 5}$."}]}
